        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Brand Deals and Section 194R Tax Rules — Free Products and Tax! (Part 2)",
        "content": "### Barter Deals Taxability and TDS Matrix\n\n| Item / Perquisite Received | Market Value | Retained or Returned? | Section 194R Applicable? | TDS Amount @ 10% | Impact on Creator's Annual Taxable Income |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Flagship Smartphone** | Rs.1,20,000 | Retained | **YES** | Rs.12,000 | + Rs.1,20,000 added to gross receipts |\n| **Editing Workstation/PC** | Rs.2,10,000 | Returned (proof of delivery) | **NO** | Rs.0 | Rs.0 (No tax impact) |\n| **Free Apparel and Makeup** | Rs.18,000 (total FY) | Retained | **NO** (Below Rs.20k limit) | Rs.0 | Rs.0 (Below threshold) |\n| **Designer Handbag** | Rs.55,000 | Retained | **YES** | Rs.5,500 | + Rs.55,000 added to gross receipts |\n| **All-Inclusive Maldives Trip** | Rs.3,20,000 | Enjoyed / Used | **YES** | Rs.32,000 | + Rs.3,20,000 added to gross receipts |\n| **Concert VIP Pass** | Rs.25,000 | Retained / Used | **YES** | Rs.2,500 | + Rs.2,500 added to gross receipts |\n| **Product Sample Goodies** | Rs.4,000 | Retained | **NO** | Rs.0 | Rs.0 |\n\n---\n\n### How Brands Deposit 194R TDS for In-Kind Products (Non-Cash Items)\n\nWhen a brand gifts a physical laptop worth Rs.1,50,000 to Shreya, there is no monetary cash transaction from which 10% TDS can be withheld directly. CBDT provides **Two Approved Methods** for handling this:\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ IN-KIND 194R TDS DEPOSITION OPTIONS                                    │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ OPTION A: Creator Pays Advance TDS Challan                             │\n│ Creator transfers Rs.15,000 (10% of Rs.1.5L) to Brand OR deposits via  │\n│ IT Challan (BSR Code + Challan No) and shares proof with Brand PR.     │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ OPTION B: Brand Pays Extra Tax (Grossing-Up Mechanism)                  │\n│ Brand pays Rs.15,000 out of its own corporate pocket to Govt as TDS.   │\n│ Benefit value grossed up in Brand's tax books.                          │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```",
        "color": "#10B981",
        "emoji": "🌐",
        "interactiveType": "no"
