        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Brand Deals and Section 194R Tax Rules — Free Products and Tax! (Part 3)",
        "content": "3. **Total TDS Credited to Shreya's Form 26AS / AIS:**\n $$\\text{Total TDS Deposited in Govt Treasury} = Rs.10,000 + Rs.15,000 = Rs.25,000$$\n\n---\n\n#### Step 2: Calculating Gross Receipts and Filing ITR-4 under Section 44ADA\n\nShreya opts for **Section 44ADA Presumptive Taxation Scheme** for professionals (Ref: **Module 13: Advanced Tax for Freelancers**).\n\n1. **Calculation of total gross receipts:**\n $$\\text{Gross Receipts} = \\text{Cash Payout Received} + \\text{Fair Market Value of Retained Goods}$$\n $$\\text{Gross Receipts} = Rs.1,00,000 + Rs.1,50,000 = Rs.2,50,000$$\n\n2. **Application of Section 44ADA 50% Presumptive Income Rule:**\n Under Section 44ADA, professionals are presumed to have incurred 50% of their gross receipts on business operational expenses without needing to maintain expense bills or receipts!\n $$\\text{Total Taxable Business Income} = 50\\% \\times \\text{Gross Receipts}$$\n $$\\text{Total Taxable Business Income} = 50\\% \\times Rs.2,50,000 = Rs.1,25,000$$\n\n---\n\n#### Step 3: Income Tax Calculation and Rebate under New Tax Regime\n\nLet us compute Shreya's final tax liability under the **New Tax Regime** (FY 2025-26):\n\n```markdown\nShreya's Tax Computation Breakdown:\n- Gross Taxable Income: Rs.1,25,000\n- Basic Exemption Limit (New Tax Regime): Rs.3,00,000\n- Tax Payable as per Slab Rates: Rs.0\n- Tax Rebate under Section 87A (Income < Rs.7,00,000): Full Rebate\n- Final Tax Payable: Rs.0.00\n```\n\n---\n\n#### Step 4: Claiming the 10% TDS Refund from Income Tax Department!\n\nShreya files her annual tax return **ITR-4 (Sugam)** before July 31st:\n- Calculated total tax liability: **Rs.0**\n- Total TDS Already Paid and recorded in Form 26AS: **Rs.25,000**\n- **Total Refund Due to Shreya:** **Rs.25,000 + Statutory interest @ 0.5% per month!**\n\n> **GOLDEN LESSON:** Thousands of student creators lose their TDS money every year because they think *\"If I don't have to pay tax, why should I file ITR?\"* If TDS was deducted from your income, filing ITR is the ONLY way to claim your refund!",
